<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Visualisation</span><span style="text-align:justify;">&#160;</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.663%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>KUBE is a multi-window application. User data can be viewed in the <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="text-decoration:none;">viewport</span></u> windows. All data in a file are structured by type. This tree structure is shown in the <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="text-decoration:none;">Entities pane</span></u>. It appears when you have an opened document. The tree shows the data structure of the active window.</p>
<p>There are many commands for manipulating appearance of the data. These commands are accessible via the main menu, tree context menu, viewport context menu, the <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="text-decoration:none;">toolbar</span></u>, and by <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="text-decoration:none;">shortcut keys</span></u>.</p>
<p>Front-facing surfaces and back-facing surfaces of scan data and meshes are displayed in different colours for better visualisation.</p>
